{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StirlingUpperBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StirlingUpperBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Stirling"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.factorial_le_stirling_upper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.factorial_le_stirling_upper","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StirlingUpperBound.lean#L44-L68","doc":"**Stirling upper bound.** For `n ≥ 1`,\n`n! ≤ e · √n · (n/e)ⁿ`. The companion of `Stirling.le_factorial_stirling`\n(which bounds `n!` from below); together they pin `n!` to `Θ(√n (n/e)ⁿ)`.\nWatson-uniqueness brick 1 — the piece Mathlib was missing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Borel.stirlingSeq_le_succ_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Borel.stirlingSeq_le_succ_zero","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StirlingUpperBound.lean#L30-L42","doc":"`stirlingSeq n ≤ e/√2` for `n ≥ 1`: the sequence `stirlingSeq` decreases\n(to `√π`), so past `n = 1` it never exceeds `stirlingSeq 1 = e/√2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}